# QEMU-boot variant config fragment (relative to la32_defconfig)
#
# Purpose (iteration 033 + 039): boot the committed kernel source on the
# official NSCSCC la32r QEMU (ls3a5k32, 128MB).  The QEMU machine does not
# model the SoC's NT35510 LCD, the UE11 USB host controller, the Altera PS/2
# serio device, or the DMFE Ethernet MAC, so those peripherals are disabled to
# reach a stable BusyBox shell.
#
# This fragment DISABLES hardware peripherals for the QEMU boot lane ONLY.
# It is NOT a board configuration and proves committed kernel source boots,
# not board peripheral function.  Board evidence requires the real handoff
# triple (see hardware-validation-candidate-426629c84.md).
#
# Apply on top of la32_defconfig:
#   make ARCH=loongarch la32_defconfig
#   scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh -m arch/loongarch/configs/la32_defconfig \
#     <this fragment>
#   make ARCH=loongarch olddefconfig
#
# SEMANTIC CLAIM: applying this fragment disables exactly the five peripherals
# below and points the embedded initramfs at the boot cpio.  It reproduces the
# iteration-033 variant INTENT plus the iteration-039 discovery that the DMFE
# Ethernet MAC is also QEMU-unmodeled.  It is NOT a byte-exact .config
# reproducer: the recorded iteration-033 .config sha256 (84c28cd...) embeds
# toolchain/build-info lines (CC_VERSION_TEXT, LOCALVERSION_AUTO,
# AUDIT/TASKSTATS/CGROUP/RD_* toggles) that came from the original build flow.
# The peripheral disables below are the load-bearing variant semantics and
# match the original build's .config exactly (verified by merge + diff).
#
# Original iteration-033 build .config sha256:
#   84c28cd81abf7f5662ad9a2efe70a64da915e37edcf5a45947247477c67a7a9c
#
# Iteration-039 update: the canonical handoff initramfs (0c18889c...) sets
# AUTO_NET=1 in /etc/nscscc/network.conf, so S40network runs `ip link set eth0
# up`.  QEMU ls3a5k32 does not model the DMFE Ethernet MAC, so dmfe_open()
# faults (iowrite32 address error) unless CONFIG_DMFE_MAC is also disabled.
# With this fifth disable the canonical initramfs boots to a / # shell
# ("Network interface not found: eth0" is the non-fatal expected message).
#
# Iteration-042 update (DS checkpoint-037-040 portability finding): the boot
# lane now embeds the COMMITTED canonical initramfs
# (Documentation/nscscc/evidence/initramfs-426629c84.cpio.gz, sha256
# 0c18889c0e4f340cb754b49becdd8cecac6c2e9a1ba71752887016b74ddeb2c6) instead of
# a host-local /tmp artifact.  CONFIG_INITRAMFS_SOURCE must resolve to the
# kernel source root: give merge_config the absolute path to the committed file
# (the fragment below records the committed-relative path as the canonical
# identity, and the build substitutes the srctree root).  This makes the lane
# reproducible from the git tree: the only external inputs are the toolchain and
# the official NSCSCC la32r QEMU wrapper (see qemu-boot-manifest-608939906.txt).

# SoC peripherals not modeled by QEMU ls3a5k32 -> disable
# CONFIG_CHIPLAB_NT35510 is not set
# CONFIG_USB_UE11_HCD is not set
# CONFIG_SERIO_ALTERA_PS2 is not set
# CONFIG_DMFE_MAC is not set

# PS/2 keyboard/atkbd has no serio source without SERIO_ALTERA_PS2
# CONFIG_KEYBOARD_ATKBD is not set

# Embedded initramfs for the boot lane (committed canonical cpio.gz)
# CONFIG_INITRAMFS_SOURCE is substituted with the srctree-rooted absolute path
# to the committed file below at build time (see iteration-042 note above).
CONFIG_INITRAMFS_SOURCE="Documentation/nscscc/evidence/initramfs-426629c84.cpio.gz"
CONFIG_INITRAMFS_COMPRESSION_GZIP=y
# CONFIG_INITRAMFS_COMPRESSION_BZIP2 is not set
# CONFIG_INITRAMFS_COMPRESSION_NONE is not set
